      "completeExpectedSpokenText": "Build a five-point checklist rather than a list of equipment names. First: the site and route are safe, with permission and utility clearance. Second: tools are sound, clean and carried safely. Third: protection matches the task and any chemical information. Fourth: the supervisor knows the location and return time, and the buddy and communication arrangements are clear. Fifth: emergency contacts, access, meeting point, water and weather precautions are known.\n\nFor each point, state what would make you stop. Examples include uncertain buried services, a loose tool handle, missing chemical information, a failed communication plan or a moving machine blocking the route. Report the problem and wait for a safe arrangement; ticking a box does not resolve a hazard.\n\nPreparation, awareness and limits reduce the chance of making a bad situation worse. Completing this step does not qualify you as a first aider or certify your physical performance. Your trainer observes the practical task separately.",
